  "body": "Fetch has two concepts we should probably be using and cross-referencing more than we currently are:\n- [Network error](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-network-error)\n- [ok status](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#ok-status)\n\nThe current spec is not consistent about how it uses these. Ctrl+F for the following strings:\n- 4xx\n- 5xx\n- network error\n- type is \"error\"\n\nMaybe Fetch should introduce a concept \"a response is **not ok** if it is a network error or its status is not an ok status\"? Then HTML could use it throughout.\n",
